            <h2>Tips for your first rehearsal room visit</h2>
            <p>If you haven't used a rehearsal room before, these tips will make your first session go smoothly:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Prepare your setlist before you arrive</strong> — deciding what to play inside the room wastes paid time. Agree on songs the day before.</li>
              <li><strong>Arrive at least 10 minutes early</strong> — use that time for setup and tuning before your booked slot starts.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring your own guitar or bass</strong> — everything else is in the room, but play on your own instrument.</li>
              <li><strong>Pack a spare cable</strong> — a dead cable in the room means the session stops. It happens more often than you'd expect.</li>
              <li><strong>Record the session</strong> — prop your phone on a stand and hit record. You'll catch timing and pitch issues that are impossible to hear while playing.</li>
              <li><strong>Ask about rates before booking</strong> — pricing varies by room size and time slot. Always confirm before you commit.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>For a complete rehearsal preparation guide, read <a href={`/${lang}/blog/how-to-prepare-for-band-rehearsal`}>How to prepare for band rehearsal</a>.</p>

            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>

            <p><strong>How much does a rehearsal room in Bangkok cost?</strong><br />Rates vary by room size, time of day, and included equipment. Contact the studio directly for current pricing.</p>

            <p><strong>Do I need to bring my own instrument?</strong><br />Bring your guitar or bass. Amps, drums, PA, and mics are included in the room.</p>

            <p><strong>How do I book?</strong><br />Contact Thunder Studio via LINE or through the booking form on the website.</p>

            <p><strong>How many people fit in a rehearsal room?</strong><br />Studio 2 fits 2-4 people. Studio 1 fits 6-10 — suitable for a full band.</p>

            <p><strong>Can I record in the rehearsal room?</strong><br />Rehearsal rooms are not designed for recording. Thunder Studio's <a href={`/${lang}/rooms/control-room`}>Control Room</a> has a mixing console and DAW workstation for dedicated recording sessions.</p>

            <p><strong>What should I bring?</strong><br />Your instrument, a spare cable, a tuner, and your setlist. Arrive 10 minutes before your slot for setup.</p>

            <p><strong>How do I get started at Thunder Studio?</strong><br />Book online or via LINE. Share your group size and preferred time — the team will recommend the right room.</p>
